This code first defines the specific components of GDP as variables. Then it calculates the Nominal GDP by summing up all the specific components.
Next, it calculates the Real GDP by dividing the Nominal GDP by a GDP deflator of 1.05. This accounts for inflation and adjusts the nominal GDP to a real GDP.
Finally, it calculates the Per Capita GDP by dividing the Real GDP by the population of the USA (328 million). This accounts for population growth and adjusts the real GDP to a per capita GDP.

