```
% Define the substitution cipher
cipher = 'EJGHBRVIUFLPNJMKOSAQWDZYXCT';
% Define the alphabet
alphabet = 'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ';
% Read in the cryptic message
message = 'EJGHBRVIUFLPNJMKOSAQWDZYXCT';
% Perform frequency analysis
frequencies = zeros(26,1);
for i = 1:length(message)
    index = find(alphabet == message(i));
    frequencies(index) = frequencies(index) + 1;
end
% Sort the frequencies in descending order
[sorted_freq, indices] = sort(frequencies, 'descend');
% Calculate the shift between the cipher and the alphabet
shift = indices - (1:26)';
% Decode the message using the shift
decoded_message = '';
for i = 1:length(message)
    index = find(cipher == message(i));
    if ~isempty(index)
        decoded_index = mod(index - shift(index) - 1, 26) + 1;
        decoded_message = [decoded_message alphabet(decoded_index)];
    else
        decoded_message = [decoded_message message(i)];
    end
end
% Display the decoded message
disp(decoded_message);
```
This code first defines the substitution cipher and the alphabet. It then reads in the cryptic message and performs frequency analysis to determine the most common letters in the message. It then calculates the shift between the cipher and the alphabet by comparing the frequencies of the letters in the message to the frequencies of the letters in the alphabet. Finally, it decodes the message using the shift and displays the decoded message.

